000200 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000300 PROGRAM-ID. TPICTURE.
000400 AUTHOR.     C HILLES.
000500 DATE-WRITTEN. AUGUST, 1984.
000600 DATE-COMPILED.
000700*INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
000800*SECURITY.
000900*REMARKS.
001000*
001100*    THIS PROGRAM WAS DEVELOPED FOR ANNUAL RAW MATERIAL INVENTORIES
001200*    AT THE MIX CENTER IN AKRON.  IT LOCKS THE STORES DATABASE AND
001300*    RUNS THROUGH "MSTORERM", AND CREATES A FILE WHICH CONTAINS
001400*    A "PICTURE" OF THE ONHAND QUANTITES AT THAT TIME.  THIS FILE
001500*    CONTAINS CORP-CODE, GENERIC NAME (IE "ADAMAX"), UM, AND
001600*    QTY ONHAND.  THIS FILE IS THEN RJEd INTO THE MAINFRAME IBM
001700*    SYSTEM FOR TAG INVENTORY COUNT ADJUSTMENTS.
001800*
      *C   09MAR1994    DAVE PLUM
      *C     ADDED CALL TO THE COBOL ERROR HANDLER - MCXCBLERR.
      *C
      *C   09SEP1996   DAVE PLUM
      *C     RECOMPILED FOR CENTURY DATABASE CHANGES.
      *C
002000 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
002100 CONFIGURATION SECTION.
002200 SOURCE-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
002300 OBJECT-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT MSTORERM-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0201
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

002900     SELECT PICTURE-FILE ASSIGN TO DISK-MCFPPICT.
003000
003100 DATA DIVISION.
003200 FILE SECTION.
003300
003400 FD  PICTURE-FILE
003500     RECORD CONTAINS 80 CHARACTERS
003600     DATA RECORD IS PICTURE-REC.
003700 01  PICTURE-REC.
003800     05  PIC-CODE                     PIC X(7).
003900     05  PIC-GENERIC-NAME             PIC X(30).
004000     05  PIC-UM                       PIC X(2).
004100     05  PIC-ONHAND                   PIC S9(8).
004200     05  PIC-FILLER                   PIC X(33).
004300
       FD  MSTORERM-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MSTORERM-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0200  OF MCFLCS0201.

004400 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       77  MCXCBLERR-SCOPE               PIC X(1)  VALUE "C".
004500
004600 01  DESC-WORK.
004700     05  DESC-WORK-KEYWORD         PIC X(20).
004800     05  DESC-WORK-ADJ             PIC X(30).
004900     05  FILLER                    PIC X(30).
005000
005100*************************************************************
005200**                                                          **
005300**          C O M M U N I C A T I O N S   A R E A S         **
005400**                                                          **
005500**************************************************************
005600
005700 COPY TBLOWUP    IN COPYLIB.
005800 COPY CDESC      IN COPYLIB.
       COPY CCRTFILE   IN COPYLIB.
005900*** PARM FOR CALL TO ANY SUBPROGRAM
006000
006100 01  RET-CODE                      PIC X(2)  VALUE SPACES.
006200
006300*** PARM FOR CALL TO "TDETCODE"
006400
006500 01  ALT-KEY                       PIC X(40).
006600**************************************************************
006700**                                                          **
006800**            D A T A B A S E   W O R K                     **
006900**                                                          **
007000**************************************************************
       01  FILE-STATUS.
           05  FILE-STATUS-1            PIC X  VALUE "0".
           05  FILE-STATUS-2            PIC X  VALUE "0".
007100
007200 01  BASE                       PIC X(10) VALUE "  STORES;".
007300 01  PASSWORD                   PIC X(8)  VALUE "JADE;   ".

007400 COPY DBSTAT     IN COPYLIB.
007500
007600 01  DB-DATASETS.
007700     05  DSET-MSTORERM          PIC X(16)  VALUE "MSTORERM;".
007800
007900 01  MODE-AREA.
008000     05  MODE1                  PIC S9(4)   COMP       VALUE 1.
008100     05  MODE2                  PIC S9(4)   COMP       VALUE 2.
008200     05  MODE3                  PIC S9(4)   COMP       VALUE 3.
008300     05  MODE7                  PIC S9(4)   COMP       VALUE 7.
008400
008500 01  CODE-SEARCH                PIC X(10) VALUE "CORP-CODE;".
008600
008700 01  CODE-ARG                   PIC X(8)  VALUE SPACES.
008800 01  LAST-LIST                  PIC X(2)  VALUE "*;".
008900 01  ALL-ITEMS                  PIC X(2)  VALUE "@;".
009000
009100**************************************************************
009200**                                                          **
009300**           D A T A B A S E   B U F F E R S                **
009400**                                                          **
009500**************************************************************
009600
009700 COPY MSTORERM   IN COPYLIB.
009800
009900 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
010000 1-HOUSEKEEP SECTION.
010100 1-BEGIN-HOUSEKEEP.
           MOVE "C" TO MCXCBLERR-SCOPE.
           CALL "MCXCBLERR" USING MCXCBLERR-SCOPE.

      *------ CALL CCRTFILE TO CREATE A TEMPORARY FILE 'XXXXXXXX'
           MOVE "*LIBL"       TO CCRTFILE-LIBRARY.
           MOVE "MCFPPICT"    TO CCRTFILE-FILE.
           MOVE "0080"        TO CCRTFILE-RECORD-LENGTH.
           MOVE "01000"       TO CCRTFILE-NO-RECORDS.
           MOVE "01000"       TO CCRTFILE-INCREMENT-AMT.
           MOVE "99"          TO CCRTFILE-NO-INCREMENTS.
           CALL "CCRTFILE" USING CCRTFILE-LIBRARY,
                                 CCRTFILE-FILE,
                                 CCRTFILE-RECORD-LENGTH,
                                 CCRTFILE-NO-RECORDS,
                                 CCRTFILE-INCREMENT-AMT,
                                 CCRTFILE-NO-INCREMENTS,
                                 CCRTFILE-STATUS.
           IF CCRTFILE-STATUS NOT = "00"
               MOVE "CCRTFILE CREATE OF 'MCFPPICT' FAILED"
                  TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
               PERFORM 2100-BLOWUP.

           OPEN INPUT MSTORERM-I.
011000     OPEN OUTPUT PICTURE-FILE.
011100
010200     MOVE SPACES                   TO   PIC-FILLER.
010300*---------- WE CANT LOOK AT LOCAL DESCRIPTION.  ONLY 1ST AND 2CD LINE
010400     MOVE "N"                      TO   CDESC-LOCAL-DESC-OPTION.
010900
011200     PERFORM 6000-MAIN THRU 6990-MAIN-X.
011300
011400 2000-EOJ.
011500     CLOSE PICTURE-FILE.
           CLOSE MSTORERM-I.
011700     GOBACK.
011800
011900 2100-BLOWUP.
012000     MOVE CORP-CODE      TO  BU-DISPLAY-FLD (1).
012100     MOVE DESC-WORK-ADJ      TO  BU-DISPLAY-FLD (2).
012200     MOVE ALT-KEY            TO  BU-DISPLAY-FLD (3).
012300     CALL "TBLOWUP" USING BASE BU-PGM-NAME STATUS-AREA
012400       DUMMY-VIEW-AREA DUMMY-KSAM-STAT BU-DISPLAY-MSG
012500       BU-DISPLAY-FLDS.
012600
012700 6000-MAIN.
012800
012900*---------- LOCK THE ENTIRE DATABASE||
013000*
           MOVE SPACES TO CORPCDE OF MSTORERM-REC-I.
           START MSTORERM-I KEY >= CORPCDE OF MSTORERM-REC-I
              INVALID KEY MOVE FILE-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS.
           IF FILE-STATUS NOT = "00"
               MOVE "START ERROR MSTORERM" TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
               PERFORM 2100-BLOWUP.

013600 6100-SERIAL-READ.
013700*    CALL "DBGET" USING BASE, DSET-MSTORERM, MODE2, STATUS-AREA,
013800*      ALL-ITEMS, BUF-MSTORERM, CODE-ARG.
           MOVE 0 TO COND-WORD.
           READ MSTORERM-I NEXT INTO BUF-MSTORERM
               AT END MOVE FILE-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS.
           IF FILE-STATUS-1 = "1"
014000         GO TO 6990-MAIN-X
014100     ELSE
014200     IF FILE-STATUS NOT = "00"
014300         MOVE "DBGET ERROR 6100-SR" TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
014400         PERFORM 2100-BLOWUP.
014500
014600     IF CORP-CODE-1-2 = "26"
014700         MOVE 1                    TO   CDESC-LINES-TO-GET
014800     ELSE
014900     IF CORP-CODE-1-2 = "27"
015000         MOVE 2                    TO   CDESC-LINES-TO-GET
015100     ELSE
015200         GO TO 6100-SERIAL-READ.
015300
015400     CALL "CDESC" USING CDESC-RET-CODE, BASE, STATUS-AREA,
015500       BU-DISPLAY-MSG, CORP-CODE, CDESC-DATA.
015600     IF BU-DISPLAY-MSG-1 NOT = SPACES
015700         PERFORM 2100-BLOWUP.
015800     MOVE CDESC (1)                TO   DESC-WORK.
015900
016000     MOVE CORP-CODE            TO   PIC-CODE.
016100     IF CORP-CODE-1-2 = "26"
016200         MOVE DESC-WORK-ADJ        TO   PIC-GENERIC-NAME
016300     ELSE
016400         CALL "TDETCODE" USING RET-CODE, CDESC (2),
016500           ALT-KEY
016600         IF ALT-KEY > SPACES
016700             MOVE ALT-KEY          TO   PIC-GENERIC-NAME
016800         ELSE
016900             MOVE DESC-WORK-ADJ    TO   PIC-GENERIC-NAME.
017000
017100     MOVE STR-UM                   TO   PIC-UM.
017200     MOVE STR-ONHAND               TO   PIC-ONHAND.
017300
017400     WRITE PICTURE-REC.
017500
017600     GO TO 6100-SERIAL-READ.
017700
017800 6990-MAIN-X.
017900     EXIT.
